<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaiyō Maru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1867">1867</a>–<a href="/years/1868">1868</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Kaiyo Maru</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kaiyō Maru was a steam frigate built in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a> and delivered in 1867, then the most powerful warship in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enomoto-takeaki">Enomoto Takeaki</a> took it north to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hokkaido">Hokkaido</a> in 1868, but it ran aground and sank in a storm off Esashi late that year. A replica now stands at Esashi.</p></div>
